    "dr_id": "DR-12",
    "disagreement_register_ref": "DIS.025",
    "ruling_text": "DR-12 (native-ratified 2026-07-17): \"the data retires the loser\" -- a winner may only be named if the empirical retrodiction score supports it; neither doctrine nor engineering decides the peak model by opinion.",
    "brief_criterion": "BRIEF_D4B.md §1 B-1: name a winner only if it beats its coverage-matched shuffled-birth control with statistical distinguishability; otherwise invoke the pre-committed no-winner branch verbatim (no forced champion).",
    "verdict": "NO_WINNER",
    "reasoning": [
      "Only pratyantar_lord has an adequate event sample (n=54 of 56 scoreable events) to support any distinguishability claim; its CRPS skill vs shuffled-birth control is negative (-0.1557), i.e. it underperforms the control on average (beats control on only 9/54 = 16.7% of events).",
      "All 12 PERMISSION contenders and hierarchical_ensemble are constrained to n=3 scored events each (see career_advancement_disclosure above) -- far too small a sample for any statistical distinguishability claim regardless of sign.",
      "The two contenders with nominally positive mean CRPS skill on their n=3 slice (planetary_return +0.203, av_threshold +0.041) each beat control on only 1 of their 3 events -- consistent with sampling noise on an n=3 slice, not a genuine effect.",
      "No formal significance test (bootstrap CI / permutation p-value) exists in the committed a3_scoring_harness modules for this run; absent that infrastructure, a claim of \"genuinely beats control\" cannot be certified for any contender at this sample size, so none is certified.",
      "midpoint_triangle and transit_kernel remain NOT-EVALUABLE this wave (CR-120/CR-121, MARSYS_DEFECT_GAP_REGISTER_v2_0.md v3.10) -- they carry no scored row in this assembly and are excluded from adjudication, not defeated."
    ],
    "disposition": "Per BRIEF_D4B.md §1 B-1 no-winner branch, verbatim: B-2's backfill (when dispatched) proceeds against the best-available model with model_confidence: none_validated stamped on every row. \"Best-available\" by data coverage (not by a certified win) is pratyantar_lord (n=54, DR-17 weighted mean 0.407, 17/54 peak grades) -- named here as the coverage-adequate candidate for B-2 to consider, not as a certified champion. Campaign close records \"no validated timing model yet -- prospective loop is the path\" as the honest finding, per BRIEF_D4B.md §1 B-1 verbatim."
